  "body": "### Summary\nAs a reader, I want the lists and the topic reader to share one visual language, so that going from the Favoris cards into a topic does not feel like changing apps.\n\n### Report\nOperator, device test 2026-11-11: the lists (Favoris, Catégories, MP) show their rows as rounded cards on a dark background (inset-grouped). The reader shows messages without cards. Going from one to the other lacks consistency.\n\n### Step 1 (this issue): mock both directions, decide nothing\nProduce screenshots, from fixtures only (no real pseudos or topic titles):\n- iPhone, light and dark, regular and compact density (#799);\n- Favoris → topic → MP conversation, for both options:\n  - **A. Messages in cards:** each message (header and body) is a rounded card like the list rows, with the same margins. The lists do not change.\n  - **B. Lists without cards:** the lists go flat, edge to edge, with separators. The reader does not change.\n\nEach option is a throwaway prototype on its own branch, never merged. Cite how legacy looks (`87fe0d1c`) for reference. Post the screenshots on this issue so the operator can choose.\n\n### Step 2 (after the operator's choice)\nA spec on this issue, then the implementation PR. It is a deliberate gap if it moves away from legacy, so it gets a `gap-new` ledger row.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
